Small Business, Anthropic's plugin for running a small business (commit 5e504ae, its version 1.35.2), in
owner/commands/ and owner/shared/. Changed for Owner:
- Each of its 44 skills is a command here: its SKILL.md is the command's COMMAND.md, with a title and an ask added
  to its frontmatter and its allowed-tools, version and compatibility lines left out, and its reference notes beside it.
- Its commands are named /owner-NAME, and one link to a sibling's page names its COMMAND.md.
- Its connector addresses (.mcp.json) are left out: the owner connects their tools in their AI app. The shared
  connector note says so, and calls the rule Owner's.
- Three paths to another skill's notes name its folder under commands/.
- cash-flow-snapshot's confidence band is a share of the expected inflows, as its own table says, where its formula
  took a share of the net; its worked example follows it, and its chat summary is a markdown table.
- The voice profile, speed-to-lead's criteria and outreach-composer's corrections are kept in the owner's notes, not
  written into the plugin's own files.
Changed for Owner 1.1 (2026-11-28):
- cash-flow-snapshot's range never assumes more collected than is owed, and with no payment history it runs from
  nobody paying to everyone paying.
- invoice-chase, with nothing connected, also asks, one at a time, for the last 14 days of payments and who usually
  pays late; its mail question is skipped when no mail is connected; its scoring names the connected ledger, not
  QuickBooks alone; its subject lines carry the currency code; and a detail the owner has not given is left as a gap.
- plan-payroll's gate has a branch for payroll covered with little to spare.
- The voice profile says what to do for an owner with no emails to give.
Each changed file says so in its first line. The rest is unchanged.

